</div>
<p>The floor footprint is only 20 × 16 = 320 sq ft, or 29.73 m². This ceiling has 25% more surface area than that footprint. Calculate the geometry rather than applying that percentage to a different roof pitch.</p>
<h2>What if the ridge is off-centre or the sides differ?</h2>
<p>Calculate each plane separately instead of doubling one side. For example, take a 6 m ridge length, equal-height wall edges, horizontal runs of 2 m and 3 m, and a rise of 1.5 m.</p>
<p>The short slope is √(2² + 1.5²) = 2.5 m. The long slope is √(3² + 1.5²) = 3.3541 m.</p>
